{"Title":"An Act exempting the position of Deputy Police Chief in the city of Amesbury from the civil service law","BillNumber":"S2924","DocketNumber":"SD3360","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BRF0","Name":"Barry R. Finegold","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BRF0","ResponseDate":"2024-07-30T09:51:00.473"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BRF0","Name":"Barry R. Finegold","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BRF0","ResponseDate":"2024-07-30T09:51:00.4733333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2924/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Finegold, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 2924) of Barry R. Finegold (with approval of the mayor and city council) for legislation to exempt the position of Deputy Police Chief in the city of Amesbury from the civil service law.  Public Service.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding any general or special law to the contrary, the position of deputy police chief in the police department of the city of Amesbury shall be exempt from chapter 31 of the General Laws.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[{"Description":"S2924 -- Amesbury","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=18984&title=S2924%20--%20Amesbury"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}